  "live_records": {
    "q-49327": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49327",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$\\int {cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x) \\\\ {cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)\\text{d}x & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)\\text{d}x-\\int 1\\cdot \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
