    "q-114441": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114441",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =[-0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
